FFUUNNCCTTIIOONNSS
     The above named functions are device dependent configuration functions.
     These routines are registered with iflib by the driver and are called
     from the corresponding iflib function to configure device specific func‐
     tions and registers.

   DDeevviiccee DDeeppeennddeenntt FFuunnccttiioonnss
   SSoofftt QQuueeuuee SSeettuupp aanndd TTeeaarrddoowwnn
           iiffddii__ttxx__qquueeuueess__aalllloocc()
           Mandatory function that is called during iflib_attach to allocate
           transmit queues.  vaddrs and paddrs are arrays of virtual and phys‐
           ical addresses respectively of the hardware transmit queues.  ntxqs
           is the number of queues per qset.  ntxqsets is the number of qsets.

           iiffddii__rrxx__qquueeuueess__aalllloocc()
           Mandatory function that is called during iflib_attach to allocate
           receive queues.  vaddrs and paddrs are arrays of virtual and physi‐
           cal addresses respectively of the hardware receive queues.  nrxqs
           is the number of queues per qset.  nrxqsets is the number of qsets.

           iiffddii__qquueeuueess__ffrreeee()
           Mandatory function that frees the allocated queues and associated
           transmit buffers.

           iiffddii__ttxxqq__sseettuupp()
           Optional function for each transmit queue that handles device spe‐
           cific initialization.

           iiffddii__rrxxqq__sseettuupp()
           Optional function for each receive queue that handles device spe‐
           cific initialization.

   DDeevviiccee SSeettuupp aanndd TTeeaarrddoowwnn
           iiffddii__aattttaacchh__pprree()
           Mandatory function implemented by the driver to perform any attach
           logic that procedes interrupt and queue allocation, queue setup,
           and interrupt assignment.

           iiffddii__aattttaacchh__ppoosstt()
           Mandatory function implemented by the driver to perform any attach
           logic that occurs after ifdi_attach_pre, and iflib's queue setup
           and MSI/MSIX(X) or legacy interrupt assignment.

           iiffddii__ddeettaacchh()
           Mandatory function that frees any resources allocated by the driver
           in ifdi_attach_pre and ifdi_attach_post.

           iiffddii__vvllaann__rreeggiisstteerr()
           Optional function called by the VLAN config eventhandler.  _v_t_a_g is
           the new VLAN tag.

           iiffddii__vvllaann__uunnrreeggiisstteerr()
           Optional function called by the VLAN unconfig eventhandler.

           iiffddii__ssuussppeenndd()
           Optional function that suspends the driver.

           iiffddii__rreessuummee()
           Optional function that resumes a driver.

   DDeevviiccee CCoonnffiigguurraattiioonn FFuunnccttiioonnss
           iiffddii__iinniitt()
           Mandatory function that will initialize and bring up the hardware.
           For example, it will reset the chip and enable the receiver unit.
           It should mark the interface running, but not active (
           IFF_DRV_RUNNING, ~IIF_DRV_OACTIVE ).

           iiffddii__ssttoopp()
           Mandatory function that should disable all traffic on the interface
           by issuing a global reset on the MAC and deallocating the TX and RX
           buffers.

           iiffddii__mmuullttii__sseett()
           Programs the interfaces multicast addresses

           iiffddii__mmeeddiiaa__ssttaattuuss()
           Media Ioctl Callback.  Function is called whenever the user queries
           the status of the interface using ifconfig(8).  The driver sets the
           appropriate link type and speed in ifmr->ifm_active.

           iiffddii__mmttuu__sseett()
           Sets the mtu interface to the value of the second function parame‐
           ter mtu.

           iiffddii__mmeeddiiaa__cchhaannggee()
           Function is called when the user changes speed/duplex using the me‐
           dia/mediaopt option with ifconfig(8).

           iiffddii__pprroommiisscc__sseett()
           Enables or disables promisc settings depending upon the flags
           value.  _f_l_a_g_s contains the interface's ifnet(9) flags.

           iiffddii__ggeett__ccoouunntteerr()
           Returns the value for counter cnt depending upon counter type.

           iiffddii__uuppddaattee__aaddmmiinn__ssttaattuuss()
           Sets the link_up state to TRUE or FALSE depending upon the OS link
           state.  A real check of the hardware only happens with a link in‐
           terrupt.

           iiffddii__mmeeddiiaa__sseett()
           Need to define

